    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-c/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-c/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\", x∈ . f x ( ) = 3sin x + cos x ( ) ( ) ( ) 3 a) Express f x in the form R cos x − α , R &gt; 0 ,  0 &lt; α &lt; 90 ° . b) State the maximum value of f x and find the smallest positive value of x ( ) for which this maximum occurs. ( ) 3 The temperature of the water T C ° in a tropical fish tank is modelled by the equation ( ) ( ) T = 32 + 3sin 15 t ° + cos 15 t °,  0 ≤&lt; t 24 , where t is the time in hours measured since midnight.\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-c/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) State the maximum temperature of the water in the tank and the time when this maximum temperature occurs. ( ) 3 d) Show that the temperature of the water in the tank reaches 30.5 C ° at 13:14 and at 18: 46 . ( ) [You may not verify the answers in this part] 6\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
